 r←Test_NeedsUser_001(stopFlag batchFlag);rc;parms;n;list;msg;⎕TRAP
⍝ Exercise "ProcessTool". There is no "Process" button. Processing is triggered via the context menu.
⍝ This cannot be fully automated since context menus are strictly modal like other menus.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 :If 1=batchFlag
     r←¯1
 :Else
     r←T._Failed
     ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
     msg←''
     msg,←⊂'Test of the context menu'
     msg,←⊂'When the context menu appears press `n` - that is the hot key for "Do it now!"'
     msg,←⊂'Note that the context menu will appear at the current position of the mouse'
     msg,←⊂'Don''t change the selection!'
     CommTools.Pause msg

     parms←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.ProcessTool.CreateParms
     parms.posn←30 40
     list←('one' 'two' 'three' 'four' 'five' 'six' 'seven' 'eight' 'nine'),[0.5]1+⍳9
     parms.default←(1+⍳9)∊3 5
     parms.style←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.Enums.SelectionStyles.multi
     parms.processBtnCaption←'Do it - now!'
     parms.info←'Checks whether the context menu works as intended'
     parms.processBtnCaption←''
     parms.contextMenuCaptions←'Do it &now!'
     n←parms #.APLGUI.APLGUI.ProcessTool.Create list'∆HarvestSelections'
     ⎕DL 0.3
     1 ⎕NQ n.List'ContextMenu'
     ∆Process n.∆Form
     →T.GoToTidyUp n.∆result≢,⊂list[3 5-1;]
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠⍴n.∆buttons
     r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
     n.∆CloseForm
 :EndIf
